{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1272192-on-the-succession-of-selkie-skins","id":1272192,"title":"On the succession of Selkie skins","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-01T09:29:29-08:00","id":1272192,"title":"On the succession of Selkie skins","content":"One of my PCs is a selkie. We decided in character creation that she got her skin from her mother (who got it from her grandmother). <br /> <br /> Now that her mom doesn't have a fae mien anymore, is she an Undone? A Kinain? Something else that's selkie-specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12930-gogariglenross","name":"GogariGlenRoss","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T09:54:36-08:00","id":1272195,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking undone, but I'm not sure what the canonical answer is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T11:03:49-08:00","id":1272211,"title":"","content":"Their write up implies that selkie grumps search for someone to inherit their skin. Appearently, selkie grumps are rare because most will pass on their skin and become undone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:44:02-07:00","id":1302176,"title":"","content":"So most of the time I would say undone. However... there is an argument to be made in this case that she stops being a changeling but could remain a kinain. She may be less aware of the dreaming of playing with the original rules (vs. The c20 kinain) as she is affected by the Mists, but as she was the child of a changeling, she may retain some touch of glamour yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}